; zero page temps (the game owns the zero page: the NMI saves/restores $F0-$FF)
; Renderer zero page: only its pointers (for (zp),Y), exchanged with the game's bytes whenever the CPU passes between the
; renderer and the game (resident.s zswap: render start/end, yield/resume; not around game IRQs, which never touch them). There are no
; free zero-page bytes to give it: these are the X/Y/direction of object slots 15-18 (NES ObjX/ObjY/ObjDir + $0F..$12:
; Link's boomerang, bombs/fire, arrow/rod), which earlier explorations without sub-weapons never saw written (HANDOFF
; bug 5: bombs landed anywhere). The scalars are plain RAM (RES9's tail).
